% ============================================================================
% gas-laws.query.adj — a worked recall over the chemistry gas-laws library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "which two quantities does
% Gay-Lussac's law relate?": it states no gas-law fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves
% each `?` against the `gas_law_relates` rows and returns the pair + the table's
% source/locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% pair `pressure_temperature`, recall which law names it — gay_lussac). A name
% that is not one of the four simple gas laws abstains honestly — the engine
% never invents a relation.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli gas-laws.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "gas-laws.adj"

? gas_law_relates(boyle, $Pair)                  % expect pressure_volume
? gas_law_relates(charles, $Pair)                % expect volume_temperature
? gas_law_relates(avogadro, $Pair)               % expect volume_moles
? gas_law_relates($Law, pressure_temperature)    % reverse bind — expect gay_lussac
? gas_law_relates(newton, $Pair)                 % expect abstain — Newton's laws are mechanics, not a gas law
